      "lineNbr": 373,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-24T15:33:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s coming from [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/ShaderModule.cpp;drc\u003d5c52321d98d5dae78b51393f35ba0db39a0b5c10;l\u003d974). IMHO the metadata should be called `usesSampleInterpolant` to be more precise, and `RenderPipeline::IsFragMultiSampled` could be `UsesSampleRateShading` and return `samplecount() \u003e 1 \u0026\u0026 (usesSampleInterpolant || usesSampleIndex || usesFramebufferFetch)`.\n\nWhat we care about is whether the fragment shader will be executing once per sample, or only once per pixel and the result broadcast to each sample. That\u0027s `UsesSampleRateShading` and the condition used for both `needsMultisampledFramebufferFetch` and `polyfillPixelCenter`.",
      "parentUuid": "ef853c88_b0f22d55",
      "revId": "92ffead253d09ba8ea5a0adc38ddd5f9e65825d4",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
